QuickSift overlay patch: upstream dav1d commit a34e0685b9111b9eb1d7835ea7bea5b425dced73
"compat: Fix building with newer versions of MSVC" (Martin Storsjo, 2026-09-09),
first released in dav1d 1.5.5 and carried by vcpkg's dav1d 1.5.4#1 (Patch Tuesday
November 2026, microsoft/vcpkg#55001). MSVC 19.52 (VS 2026 18.12) rejects the
undefined function-like macro __has_include_next in the compat <stdatomic.h> #if
(error C7780 / C1017); a fallback definition lets the expression evaluate to 0.
The compat header is only used for MSVC builds where cl lacks <stdatomic.h>.

diff --git a/include/compat/msvc/stdatomic.h b/include/compat/msvc/stdatomic.h
index 618f0ee87dbd1c4818f1a3e05781062addd81c99..d637daa5c4cc575affb6d416fa01a6829fd49a72 100644
--- a/include/compat/msvc/stdatomic.h
+++ b/include/compat/msvc/stdatomic.h
@@ -32,6 +32,10 @@
 #pragma warning(push)
 #pragma warning(disable:4067)    /* newline for __has_include_next */
 
+#ifndef __has_include_next
+#define __has_include_next(x) 0
+#endif
+
 #if defined(__clang__) && __has_include_next(<stdatomic.h>)
    /* use the clang stdatomic.h with clang-cl*/
 #  include_next <stdatomic.h>
